<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of La Tour d'Auvergne</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as La Tour d'Auvergne</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The La Tour d'Auvergne were a French noble family named after La Tour in Auvergne. By marriage they acquired the counties of Auvergne and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boulogne-sur-mer">Boulogne</a> in the late 14th century, and in 1444 the Viscounty of Turenne. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madeleine-de-la-tour-dauvergne">Madeleine de La Tour d'Auvergne</a> was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-de-medici">Catherine de' Medici</a>. Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne married the heiress of the La Marck, becoming prince of Sedan and duke of Bouillon; his son was Marshal Turenne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-la-tour-dauvergne.jpg" alt="House of La Tour d'Auvergne" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_Emmanuel_Th%C3%A9odose_de_La_Tour_de_Bouillon_(1647-1715).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The remaining county, centred on Vic-le-Comte, passed to the <b>La Tour</b> family and through Madeleine de la Tour d'Auvergne to her daughter Catherine de' Medici.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-auvergne">County of Auvergne</a></li><li><blockquote>The county passed through the houses of Auvergne and <b>La Tour</b> before the Burgundian State took it in 1435.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-boulogne">County of Boulogne</a></li><li><blockquote>Possession was contested between the La Marcks, their <b>La Tour d'Auvergne</b> heirs and Liège.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-bouillon">Duchy of Bouillon</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1444 the viscounty passed to the <b>La Tour d'Auvergne</b> family.</blockquote><a href="/state/viscounty-of-turenne">Viscounty of Turenne</a></li></ul></section>
